                <pb facs="pm_d9-1" n="1" xml:id="pm_d9-1"/>

                <head>PM–9. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On December 18, 1958, the National Assembly of Panama enacted Law No. 58 which
                    extended to twelve miles the breadth of the territorial waters of the Republic
                    of Panama. Responding on January 9, 1959, the Department of State, through the
                    Embassy at Panama City, protested this action and informed the Ministry of
                    Foreign Relations that the United States Government was under no obligation to
                    recognize a territorial sea limit of more than three miles and hoped that the
                        <pb facs="0982" n="894" type="typeset" xml:id="pg894"/> Republic of Panama
                    would reconsider its action. In its reply of January 21, 1959, the Ministry of
                    Foreign Relations rejected the arguments that the Embassy had advanced in its
                    note of January 9. Documentation on this subject is in decimal file 719.022.</p>
            </div>
